# mount(1)

## NAME

mount - mount a disk or list mounts

## SYNOPSIS

    mount
    mount -l
    mount [-r|-w] disk dir

## DESCRIPTION

Without arguments, lists mounts in the order they were added, as `source on dir type kind (ro|rw)`.

With a disk and a directory, mounts the disk (`disk:ID`; `disk:` is added if missing) on the directory. The directory does not need to exist.

## OPTIONS

- `-l`: list inserted disks with their size, entry count and mount point
- `-r`: mount read-only
- `-w`: mount read-write (the default)

## SEE ALSO

umount(1), df(1)
